WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: fr

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:06.239
.

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:07.274 size:53% position:73% line:53%
♪ ♪ ♪

00:00:05.539 --> 00:00:08.275 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Howie Morenz,

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.309 size:53% position:73% line:53%
the Babe Ruth of hockey.

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:10.343 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- En 1931, au tout nouveau Maple

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:11.378 size:53% position:73% line:53%
Leaf Gardens, une foule record

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:12.412 size:53% position:73% line:53%
de plus de 15 000 spectateurs

00:00:10.644 --> 00:00:15.916 size:53% position:73% line:53%
assistent à un match entre

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:16.917 size:53% position:73% line:53%
les deux équipes canadiennes

00:00:12.713 --> 00:00:17.918 size:53% position:73% line:53%
les plus célèbres.

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:18.952 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Two great teams battling it

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:19.986 size:53% position:73% line:53%
out for supremacy.

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:22.956 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Une rivalité légendaire

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:26.226 size:53% position:73% line:53%
est née.

00:00:20.287 --> 00:00:27.227 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- This is the playoff!

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:33.934 size:53% position:73% line:53%
♪ ♪ ♪

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:34.935 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Toronto et Montréal se livrent

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:35.969 size:53% position:73% line:53%
des batailles mémorables.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:37.003 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- The fans are in a frenzy.

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:38.038 size:53% position:73% line:53%
Every game of séries

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:39.072 size:53% position:73% line:53%
has gone into overtime.

00:00:37.304 --> 00:00:40.073 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- En 1951, les Maple Leafs

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:41.107 size:53% position:73% line:53%
battent les Canadiens

00:00:39.373 --> 00:00:42.142 size:53% position:73% line:53%
en finale, mais Montréal

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:43.176 size:53% position:73% line:53%
prépare sa revanche.

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:44.211 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Three seconds to go,

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:46.613 size:53% position:73% line:53%
into the corner, here

00:00:43.477 --> 00:00:47.614 size:53% position:73% line:53%
he comes, the game is over.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:48.682 size:53% position:73% line:53%
Canadiens win the Stanley Cup!

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.683 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- C'est contre les Maple Leafs

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:50.751 size:53% position:73% line:53%
que les Glorieux remportent

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:51.785 size:53% position:73% line:53%
leurs 4e et 5e coupes Stanley

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:52.819 size:53% position:73% line:53%
d'affilée, en 1959 et 60.

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:53.854 size:53% position:73% line:53%
Et c'est très valorisant de

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:54.888 size:53% position:73% line:53%
savourer la victoire devant

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.889 size:53% position:73% line:53%
l'ennemi juré de Toronto.

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:56.923 size:53% position:73% line:53%
TOE BLAKE, entraîneur-chef,

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:57.958 size:53% position:73% line:53%
Canadiens de Montréal

00:00:56.189 --> 00:01:03.830 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- J'ai jamais été si content

00:00:57.224 --> 00:01:04.865 size:53% position:73% line:53%
de toute ma vie pour avoir

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:05.866 size:53% position:73% line:53%
gagné ce championnat.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.900 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Les confrontations Toronto-

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:07.934 size:53% position:73% line:53%
Montréal ont toujours la cote.

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:08.969 size:53% position:73% line:53%
Des événements historiques

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.003 size:53% position:73% line:53%
s'y produisent.

00:01:08.235 --> 00:01:11.037 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Et pour la première fois

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:12.038 size:53% position:73% line:53%
dans l'histoire, un gardien

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:13.073 size:53% position:73% line:53%
de but porte un masque

00:01:11.338 --> 00:01:14.074 size:53% position:73% line:53%
en séries éliminatoires.

00:01:12.339 --> 00:01:16.877 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Outre Jacques Plante,

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:17.878 size:53% position:73% line:53%
Maurice Richard

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:18.912 size:53% position:73% line:53%
s'illustre aussi.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:19.946 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Maurice is right in front

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:20.981 size:53% position:73% line:53%
and he scores!

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:22.015 size:53% position:73% line:53%
(cris de la foule)

00:01:20.247 --> 00:01:25.352 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Le Rocket a déjà inscrit

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:26.353 size:53% position:73% line:53%
cinq buts lors d'un match

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:27.354 size:53% position:73% line:53%
éliminatoire contre Toronto.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:28.388 size:53% position:73% line:53%
 Quand aux Leafs, c'est contre

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:32.459 size:53% position:73% line:53%
le CH qu'ils ont gagné la Coupe

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:33.460 size:53% position:73% line:53%
Stanley pour la dernière fois,

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:34.494 size:53% position:73% line:53%
en 1967.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:35.529 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- The Toronto Maple Leafs

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.563 size:53% position:73% line:53%
have won the Stanley Cup!

00:01:34.795 --> 00:01:37.564 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Le Tricolore détient

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:38.598 size:53% position:73% line:53%
un mince avantage de 8 victoires

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:39.633 size:53% position:73% line:53%
en 15 séries contre Toronto,

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:40.667 size:53% position:73% line:53%
mais les deux derniers

00:01:38.899 --> 00:01:41.701 size:53% position:73% line:53%
affrontements se sont

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:42.736 size:53% position:73% line:53%
soldés par des balayages.

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:43.770 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Et le but!

00:01:42.002 --> 00:01:44.805 size:53% position:73% line:53%
(cris de la foule)

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:45.839 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Eh bien, voilà...

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:53.246 size:53% position:73% line:53%
le moment dramatique!

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:54.247 size:53% position:73% line:53%
Les Leafs sont terrassés;

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:55.282 size:53% position:73% line:53%
les Canadiens jubilent.

00:01:53.547 --> 00:01:56.316 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Des victoires qui

00:01:54.548 --> 00:01:57.350 size:53% position:73% line:53%
remontent à 1978 et 79.

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:58.385 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Larry Robinson, le héros!

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:59.386 size:53% position:73% line:53%
(cris de la foule)

00:01:57.651 --> 00:02:06.026 size:53% position:73% line:53%
- Un duel Toronto-Montréal qui

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:07.026 size:53% position:73% line:53%
avait pris fin dans le désordre.

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:08.061 size:53% position:73% line:53%
Larry Robinson, forcé de calmer

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:09.095 size:53% position:73% line:53%
Tiger Williams, qui voulait

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:10.096 size:53% position:73% line:53%
s'en prendre à l'officiel qui

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:13.900 size:53% position:73% line:53%
l'avait puni en prolongation.

00:02:09.396 --> 00:02:14.901 size:53% position:73% line:53%
Il a fallu attendre 42 ans pour

00:02:10.397 --> 00:02:15.368 size:53% position:73% line:53%
assister au prochain épisode.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.368 size:53% position:73% line:53%
 Ici Jean-François Poirier,

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:15.368 size:53% position:73% line:53%
 Radio-Canada, M

